# Listen — control Claude voice readback

This skill controls Listen-Claude, a TTS plugin that reads Claude's responses aloud through the system speakers (triggered by the Stop hook).

The user's intent is encoded in the argument. Two groups:

**On/off:**

| Arg | Action |
|-----|--------|
| (none) | toggle current state |
| `on` | force enable |
| `off` | force disable |
| `status` | report state without changing |

**Reading mode** (how each response is rewritten for speech):

| Arg | Effect | Underlying `TTS_MODE` |
|-----|--------|-----------------------|
| `llm` / `smart` | Claude-rewritten natural spoken summary, no markdown/symbols (~$0.001 / response, +3-8s latency) | `llm` |
| `brief` / `short` | only the opening paragraph (heuristic) | `first` |
| `progress` | opening + first ~4 bullets (heuristic, default) | `progress` |
| `summary` | first sentence of every paragraph + headings (heuristic) | `summary` |
| `detailed` / `long` | read the entire response | `full` |
| `mode` | report current mode without changing | — |

Mode changes are written to `.env` and take effect on the next Claude response — no restart needed.

## How to invoke

Run the platform-appropriate script with the arg, then echo back the script's single-line output. Nothing more.

**Windows:**
```
powershell -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File "__REPO_DIR__\scripts\toggle.ps1" __ACTION__
```

**macOS / Linux:**
```
bash "__REPO_DIR__/scripts/toggle.sh" __ACTION__
```

Replace `__ACTION__` with the user's argument (omit if no arg given — defaults to on/off toggle). The script prints either `Listen-Claude TTS: ON|OFF` or `Listen-Claude mode: <mode>` depending on which arg was used.
